From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FastPDF contributor <replace-me@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:45:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_windows: Skip the font update check when creating the text system

GetSystemFontCollection(checkForUpdates = true) makes DirectWrite check
the system font set before it answers. When the text system is created
at start-up, that took 27-38 ms on the main thread in our measurements;
without the check the call returns in under 1 ms.

The factory was created a moment earlier, so its collection is current,
and DirectWrite still applies changes that the font cache service
reports. Fonts installed while the app runs are also picked up by
select_and_cache_font, which retries with the update check when a font
is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs b/crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs
index 304dc38..639dc25 100644
--- a/crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs
@@ -195,9 +195,13 @@ impl DirectWriteTextSystem {
 
         let system_font_collection = unsafe {
             let mut result = None;
+            // No immediate update check: the factory was just created, so its
+            // collection is current, and the check costs tens of
+            // milliseconds at start-up. Fonts installed later are picked up
+            // by `select_and_cache_font`, which checks when a font is missing.
             components
                 .factory
-                .GetSystemFontCollection(false, &mut result, true)?;
+                .GetSystemFontCollection(false, &mut result, false)?;
             result.context("Failed to get system font collection")?
         };
         let custom_font_set = unsafe { components.builder.CreateFontSet()? };
